Dual-Occupancy Reality Model / Lucid State Governor

0. Claims boundary

```text
OBSERVED:
  A person can retain reasoning, language, technical skill, and partial insight
  while some perceptions, salience assignments, or beliefs are distorted.

OBSERVED:
  Lucid dreaming combines an internally generated dream world with awareness
  that the current experience is a dream.

INFERRED:
  Both phenomena can be represented by a shared dual-occupancy architecture:
  an experience-generating layer plus a model-observing layer.

EXECUTED:
  src/pantheon_prime/dual_occupancy.py implements the normalized state,
  descriptive regimes, consequence-aware Governor, and latent-skill ODE.

SPECULATIVE:
  Parameter values and regime thresholds may become empirically calibratable.
  Current thresholds are transparent engineering choices, not medical cutoffs.
```

This artifact is a formal control model, not a diagnostic instrument.
“Lucid psychosis” is retained only as the originating informal phrase. The
implementation uses preserved_insight_wakeful_distortion because lucidity,
wakefulness, distortion, diagnosis, and control are different variables.

1. Separation laws

Let

[
C_t=\text{general cognitive capability},\qquad
K_t=\text{reality-model calibration}.
]

Then the first invariant is

[
\boxed{C_t\not\equiv K_t}
]

and therefore

[
C_t\uparrow;\not\Rightarrow;K_t\uparrow.
]

A system can solve equations, speak coherently, plan efficiently, and still
execute from a locally miscalibrated premise. Capability controls the strength
of execution; calibration controls whether the execution begins from a map
that continues to update against territory.

The second invariant separates awareness from revisability:

[
\boxed{\text{recognition of alteration}\not\equiv
\text{successful correction of alteration}}
]

2. State tensor

Define the normalized state

[
\mathbf z_t=
\begin{bmatrix}
E_t&G_t&S_t&O_t&V_t&A_t&U_t&C_t
\end{bmatrix}^{!\top}\in[0,1]^8
]

with:

```text
E = external coupling: access to independent sensory/social correction
G = generative gain: strength of internally generated models
S = salience gain: felt importance or signal amplification
O = observer awareness: recognition that the model may be altered
V = revisability: actual updating when evidence pushes back
A = anchor redundancy: number/independence of reality checks
U = action urgency: pressure to convert interpretation into action
C = general capability: reasoning, memory, language, mathematics, planning
```

The variables are axes, not identities. No single coordinate diagnoses a
person, and no scalar collapses the whole state without loss.

3. Experienced-reality fusion

Let (x_t) be external state, (y_t=h(x_t)+\epsilon_t) incoming evidence,
and (m_t) the internally generated model. A minimal fusion equation is

[
\hat r_t
=\Phi!\left(
\alpha_t y_t+(1-\alpha_t)g(m_t)
\right),
]

where

[
\alpha_t=
\frac{E_tA_tV_t}
{E_tA_tV_t+G_tS_t+\varepsilon}.
]

Φ is the narrative-collapse/interface operator inherited from the Reality
Model Equation. As (EAV) increases, independent correction exerts more
influence. As (GS) increases, internally generated structure exerts more
influence. This is a control abstraction; it does not claim that subjective
experience is literally a linear mixture.

4. Dual occupancy and genuine lucidity

Dual occupancy requires two simultaneous processes:

[
\mathcal D_t=
\underbrace{\hat r_t}{\text{inhabited experience}}
\oplus
\underbrace{q_t(\hat r_t)}{\text{observer model}}.
]

Awareness alone is insufficient. Define operational lucidity as

[
\boxed{L_t=\sqrt{O_tV_t}}.
]

The geometric mean makes lucidity fall when either introspective awareness or
evidence-responsive revision is weak. The observer must do more than announce
its presence; it must permit the map to change.

Independent correction capacity is

[
Q_t=E_tA_tV_t,
]

internal dominance is

[
D_t=G_tS_t,
]

and interpretation-capture pressure is

[
P_t=\operatorname{clip}_{[0,1]}
\left[D_t\left(1-\frac{Q_t+L_t}{2}\right)\right].
]

P does not measure truth or illness. It estimates the control risk that one
internally generated interpretation may outrun available correction.

5. Lucid dream versus preserved-insight wakeful distortion

The shared invariant is

[
\text{generated experience}+\text{retained observer}.
]

The separating variable is external coupling:

[
\begin{aligned}
\text{lucid dream-like:}
&\quad E_t\downarrow,;D_t\uparrow,;L_t\uparrow,\
\text{preserved-insight wakeful distortion:}
&\quad E_t>0,;D_t\uparrow,;L_t>0,;Q_t\text{ variable}.
\end{aligned}
]

In dreaming, low external coupling is expected because the system is asleep.
In a wakeful distortion, the external world remains available and competes
with the generated model. Consequently:

[
\boxed{
\text{dream lucidity}\Rightarrow\text{possible freedom inside the dream}
}
]

while

[
\boxed{
\text{wakeful lucidity}\Rightarrow\text{greater caution before external action}
}.
]

6. Regime map

```pseudocode
function DESCRIBE(z):
    D <- z.generative_gain * z.salience_gain
    L <- sqrt(z.observer_awareness * z.revisability)
    Q <- z.external_coupling * z.anchor_redundancy * z.revisability

    if external_coupling is LOW and D is HIGH:
        if L is HIGH: return LUCID_DREAM_LIKE
        else:         return NONLUCID_DREAM_LIKE

    if external_coupling is PRESENT and D is HIGH:
        if L is PRESENT: return PRESERVED_INSIGHT_WAKEFUL_DISTORTION
        else:            return CAPTURE_RISK

    if external_coupling is HIGH and Q is ADEQUATE and D is MODERATE:
        return ORDINARY_WAKING

    return MIXED_OR_UNRESOLVED
```

These are descriptive state-space regions. They are deliberately not clinical
labels. The executable thresholds are test fixtures pending external evidence.

7. Lucid State Governor

Let an action (a) have consequence (c(a)\in[0,1]), reversibility
(r(a)\in{0,1}), and independent verification
(v(a)\in{0,1}). Define action exposure:

[
X(a,t)=c(a),[1-r(a)],[1-v(a)],[1-Q_t],[1-L_t].
]

The exact product is a diagnostic trace, not the only gate. Pantheon uses
lexicographic invariants so one low factor cannot hide a decisive hazard.

```pseudocode
function LUCID_STATE_GOVERNOR(z, action):
    assert capability(z) DOES_NOT_BYPASS calibration_gate

    reasons <- []

    if action.consequence >= HIGH and not action.reversible:
        reasons += "high-consequence action is not reversible"

    if action.consequence >= MATERIAL and not action.independently_verified:
        reasons += "premise lacks independent verification"

    if capture_pressure(z) >= LIMIT:
        reasons += "interpretation outruns correction capacity"

    if z.action_urgency >= HIGH and lucidity(z) < REQUIRED:
        reasons += "urgency exceeds current metacognitive lucidity"

    if reasons is empty:
        return ALLOW_REVERSIBLE

    if wakeful_distortion(z) or anchors(z) are sparse:
        return REQUIRE_EXTERNAL_ANCHOR(reasons)

    return DELAY_AND_CHECK(reasons)
```

External anchor protocol:

```pseudocode
PAUSE consequential action
WRITE the claim and at least two live alternatives
PREDICT evidence expected under each alternative
CHECK against independent people, instruments, records, or elapsed time
MEASURE prediction-versus-observation delta
UPDATE confidence downward as readily as upward
ACT only inside authority, reversibility, and consequence bounds
```

The Dove of Hope is the positive handle: when the local map may be flooded,
send a scout outside the frame and require a provenance-bearing return token.

8. Latent competence: the differential-equations example

Let (k\in[0,1]) be stored competence and (a(t)\in[0,1]) current active
access. Disuse can lower (a) without erasing (k). With practice intensity
(p(t)), reactivation rate (\rho), and decay rate (\mu):

[
\boxed{
\frac{da}{dt}
=\rho p(t)[k-a(t)]-\mu[1-p(t)]a(t)
}
]

The first term restores access toward the latent ceiling; the second models
retrieval decay during disuse. Thus:

[
\text{not actively remembered}\not\Rightarrow\text{never learned},
]

and relearning from latent structure should generally be faster than learning
from an unstructured zero state.

This submodel also prevents a category error in state assessment:

[
\boxed{
\text{technical competence retained}\not\Rightarrow
\text{every current premise calibrated}
}.
]

9. Delta Calculus

For claim (H_i), preserve alternatives rather than prematurely collapsing:

[
\mathcal H_t={(H_i,w_i)}_{i=1}^{n},\qquad \sum_i w_i=1.
]

After observation (o_{t+1}):

[
\delta_{i,t+1}=d!\left(\hat o_{i,t+1},o_{t+1}\right),
]

[
w_{i,t+1}
=\frac{w_{i,t}\exp(-\beta\delta_{i,t+1})}
{\sum_j w_{j,t}\exp(-\beta\delta_{j,t+1})}.
]

A model is operationally revisable when persistent adverse deltas reduce its
weight. A self-sealing model instead explains every possible result as further
confirmation:

[
\forall o,;P(o\mid H)=1
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
H\text{ is not doing discriminative predictive work}.
]

10. Invariants

```text
I-1  Capability is independent of calibration.
I-2  Coherence is not proof.
I-3  Observer awareness is not sufficient without revisability.
I-4  Missing external correction is not confirming evidence.
I-5  Felt salience is data about state, not automatic evidence about cause.
I-6  Consequence raises the required verification threshold.
I-7  Irreversibility raises the required verification threshold.
I-8  No internally generated authority can waive the external action gate.
I-9  A preserved-insight state may still require an external anchor.
I-10 The model describes state coordinates; it does not diagnose a person.
```

